// UniFFI needs a namespace declaration to generate scaffolding at all, but
// every type and interface in this crate is defined with proc-macro
// attributes in Rust (`#[derive(uniffi::Record)]`, `#[derive(uniffi::Object)]`,
// `#[uniffi::export]`, `#[uniffi::export(with_foreign)]`) rather than
// declared here a second time: declaring a type both ways produces two
// conflicting `FfiConverter` implementations for it, one from this file's
// generated scaffolding and one from the derive. See `src/types.rs`,
// `src/engine.rs`, `src/delegate.rs` and `src/events.rs` for the actual
// interface; this file stays close to empty for as long as that stays the
// chosen approach.
namespace openimzo {
};
